After applying patch3 , I discovered that it wouldn't
compile. The compiler insisted that set_omask was an unidentified
function.After some doublechecking I discovered that while
mkobj.c didn't need the function set_omask ,
pickup.c still did.
So to fix this minor bug in this large very bugfree game???
You would have to include the line

E void set_omask P((xchar,xchar));

in extern.h in a suitable place.
( I don't think this really is necessary,but for the sake.)
The following code fragment can be included either in mkobj.c
where it originally were, or in pickup.c where it is needed.

set_omask(x, y)
register xchar x, y;
{
	  levl[x][y].gmask = (g_at(x, y) != (struct gold *)0);
	  levl[x][y].omask = (o_at(x, y) != (struct obj *)0);
}

